@startuml chunk_completion_flow
'
' Chunk-completion flow — what happens when the endpoints that call
' notify_completion fire, traced per fleet.
'
' Two trigger endpoints land in the same orchestration chain:
'   PUT  /jobs/{id}/status         (community: worker self-reports done)
'   POST /jobs/{id}/register-outputs (all fleets: worker uploaded last frame)
'
' Both paths converge into RenderLifecycle.handle_chunk_succeeded.
' Per-fleet differences are isolated to two steps:
'   - The provider cancel (step 6a) — different per fleet, expensive
'   - The community-only machine flip (step 7)
'

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Inter, Helvetica, sans-serif"

' ============================================================
' Class diagram — components and ownership
' ============================================================

package "HTTP layer" #DDEEFF {
  class "jobs.py router" as Router {
    + PUT /jobs/{id}/status
    + POST /jobs/{id}/register-outputs
  }
}

package "service" #DDFFDD {
  class JobService {
    + update_status(id, status, error)
    + register_outputs(id, filenames)
    + notify_completion(id)
    -- internals --
    - _success_notifier  : Callable
  }
  note right of JobService::notify_completion
    One-line method.  Delegates to
    success_notifier (a lambda from
    bootstrap that calls
    callback_router.route(SUCCESS)).
    "notify" is a misnomer — this is
    the entry point for the entire
    chunk-completion lifecycle.
  end note
}

package "callbacks" #FFEEDD {
  class CallbackRouter {
    + route(job_id, outcome, error?)
    -- early-out --
    is_job_terminal(id) ?
  }
  class SuccessHandler {
    + handle(job_id, group_id="")
  }

  CallbackRouter --> SuccessHandler : SUCCESS path
}

package "orchestrator" #FFDDDD {
  class RenderOrchestrator {
    + on_job_succeeded(id)
    + on_job_failed(id, err)
    + is_job_terminal(id)
  }
  class RenderLifecycle {
    + handle_chunk_succeeded(id)
    + reconcile_group_status(gid)
    -- helpers --
    - _record_telemetry(...)
    - _write_terminal_snapshot(...)
  }

  RenderOrchestrator --> RenderLifecycle
}

package "fleet strategies" #EEDDFF {
  interface FleetStrategy {
    + cancel(provider_job_id)
    + stop_monitoring(job_id)
    + dispatch(...)
  }
  class VastFleetStrategy
  class ModalFleetStrategy
  class CommunityStrategy

  VastFleetStrategy ..|> FleetStrategy
  ModalFleetStrategy ..|> FleetStrategy
  CommunityStrategy ..|> FleetStrategy
}

package "fleet clients" #FFE4FF {
  class VastClient {
    + destroy(instance_id)
  }
  note right of VastClient::destroy
    httpx DELETE, timeout=30s
  end note
  class ModalClient {
    + cancel_job(provider_job_id)
  }
  note right of ModalClient::cancel_job
    Modal SDK gRPC call
    (no httpx timeout to cap)
  end note

  VastFleetStrategy --> VastClient
  ModalFleetStrategy --> ModalClient
}

package "repositories" #EEEEEE {
  class JobRepository
  class RenderGroupRepository
  class InProgressChunkRepository
  class OutputFrameRepository
  class TelemetryRepository
  class MachineRepository <<community only>>
  class PendingAllocationRepository
}

Router --> JobService : update_status / register_outputs
JobService --> CallbackRouter : success_notifier(jid)
CallbackRouter --> RenderOrchestrator : on_job_succeeded
RenderLifecycle --> JobRepository
RenderLifecycle --> RenderGroupRepository
RenderLifecycle --> InProgressChunkRepository
RenderLifecycle --> OutputFrameRepository
RenderLifecycle --> TelemetryRepository
RenderLifecycle --> PendingAllocationRepository
RenderLifecycle --> MachineRepository : community only
RenderLifecycle --> FleetStrategy : eager cancel + stop_monitoring

@enduml


' ============================================================
' Sequence — Vast fleet
' ============================================================

@startuml chunk_completion_vast

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
title Chunk completion — **Vast** fleet

actor "Vast worker" as W
participant "POST /register-outputs" as R
participant "JobService" as JS
participant "CallbackRouter" as CR
participant "RenderLifecycle" as RL
participant "VastFleetStrategy" as VS
participant "VastClient" as VC
database "Postgres" as PG
database "Redis" as RD
participant "Vast.ai API" as VAST

W ->> R : POST register-outputs (last frame)
R -> JS : register_outputs(id, files)
JS -> PG : INSERT output_frames\nupdate progress
JS --> R : completion_reached=True

R -> JS : notify_completion(id)
JS -> CR : route(SUCCESS)
CR -> CR : is_job_terminal? (PG read)
CR -> RL : handle_chunk_succeeded(id)

RL -> PG : get_raw_by_id(id)
note right: redundant w/ is_job_terminal\n(both load same row)

RL -> PG : in_progress.release(group, chunk)
RL -> PG : **mark_done(id)** -- status=done **(early!)**
note right
  After this point, any concurrent
  monitor tick reading the job
  sees status=done and exits
  cleanly via the success path.
end note

== Eager provider cleanup (step 6a) ==
RL -> VS : cancel(vast_job_id)
VS -> VC : destroy(instance_id)
VC ->> VAST : **httpx DELETE /instances/{id}**\ntimeout=30s
note right: 5–30 s under load.\nThis is the slow part\nof the entire chain.
VAST -->> VC : 200 / 204
VC --> VS
VS --> RL

RL -> VS : stop_monitoring(id)
note right: kills per-job monitor\nthread (in-process). <1ms

RL -> PG : INSERT render_telemetry

== Group rollup (step 9) ==
RL -> PG : group + jobs + output_frames + pending_alloc reads (4 queries)
RL -> RL : compute_group_status (pure)
alt status changed
  RL -> PG : update render_groups.status
  alt terminal (done/failed)
    RL -> PG : write_terminal_snapshot (3 queries)
  end
end

RL --> CR
CR --> JS
JS --> R
R -->> W : 200 OK (or worker has timed out at 30s — server still finishes)

note over W, VAST
  **No drain step.**  The
  AllocationDispatchQueueDaemon
  picks up the freed cap headroom
  on its next ~2 s tick.
end note

@enduml


' ============================================================
' Sequence — Modal fleet
' ============================================================

@startuml chunk_completion_modal

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
title Chunk completion — **Modal** fleet

actor "Modal worker" as W
participant "POST /register-outputs" as R
participant "JobService" as JS
participant "CallbackRouter" as CR
participant "RenderLifecycle" as RL
participant "ModalFleetStrategy" as MS
participant "ModalClient" as MC
database "Postgres" as PG
database "Redis" as RD
participant "Modal control plane" as MOD

W ->> R : POST register-outputs (last frame)
R -> JS : register_outputs(id, files)
JS -> PG : INSERT output_frames\nupdate progress
JS --> R : completion_reached=True

R -> JS : notify_completion(id)
JS -> CR : route(SUCCESS)
CR -> CR : is_job_terminal? (PG read)
CR -> RL : handle_chunk_succeeded(id)

RL -> PG : get_raw_by_id(id)
RL -> RL : _fire_modal_terminal_hook_if_modal
RL -> RD : ZREM modal active_jobs

RL -> PG : in_progress.release(group, chunk)
RL -> PG : **mark_done(id)** -- status=done **(early!)**

== Eager provider cleanup (step 6a) ==
RL -> MS : cancel(modal_function_call_id)
MS -> MC : cancel_job(fc-...)
MC ->> MOD : **modal.FunctionCall\n.from_id(id).cancel()**\n(gRPC, no http timeout)
note right: 5–20 s typical.\nNo httpx timeout to cap;\nrelies on Modal SDK's\ninternal timeouts.
MOD -->> MC
MC --> MS
MS --> RL

RL -> MS : stop_monitoring(id)
note right: kills per-job ModalJobMonitor\nthread. <1ms

RL -> PG : INSERT render_telemetry

== Group rollup (step 9) ==
RL -> PG : group + jobs + output_frames + pending_alloc reads (4 queries)
RL -> RL : compute_group_status (pure)
alt status changed
  RL -> PG : update render_groups.status
  alt terminal
    RL -> PG : write_terminal_snapshot (3 queries)
  end
end

RL --> CR
CR --> JS
JS --> R
R -->> W : 200 OK (or timed out; server still finishes)

note over W, MOD
  Same shape as Vast.  Differences:
  • Adds Redis ZREM on Modal active_jobs tracker
  • Cancel is gRPC (Modal SDK), not httpx
end note

@enduml


' ============================================================
' Sequence — Community fleet
' ============================================================

@startuml chunk_completion_community

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
title Chunk completion — **Community** fleet (desktop agent)

actor "Desktop agent" as W
participant "PUT /jobs/{id}/status\nor\nPOST /register-outputs" as R
participant "JobService" as JS
participant "CallbackRouter" as CR
participant "RenderLifecycle" as RL
participant "CommunityStrategy" as CS
database "Postgres" as PG
database "Redis" as RD

W ->> R : PUT status=done (with output_files)\nor POST register-outputs (last frame)
R -> JS : update_status / register_outputs
JS -> PG : INSERT output_frames\nupdate progress\nset jobs.status=done (status path)
JS --> R : needs_completion / completion_reached = True

R -> JS : notify_completion(id)
JS -> CR : route(SUCCESS)
CR -> CR : is_job_terminal? (PG read)
note right of CR
  On the status=done path the row
  is **already** terminal here, so
  the chain short-circuits.  This
  is fine — the heavy work
  happened inline in update_status.
end note
CR -> RL : handle_chunk_succeeded(id)\n(only if not already terminal)

RL -> PG : get_raw_by_id(id)
RL -> PG : in_progress.release(group, chunk)
RL -> PG : mark_done(id)

== Eager provider cleanup (step 6a) ==
RL -> CS : cancel(provider_job_id="")
note right: **No-op for community.**\nNo provider, no API to call.\nstrategy.cancel short-circuits\non empty provider_job_id.
RL -> CS : stop_monitoring(id)
note right: Community uses singleton\nCommunityMonitor — no per-job\nthread to stop.  Also a no-op.

== Community-only step 7 ==
RL -> PG : machine_repo.update_status(\nmachine_id, 'available')
note right
  Vast/Modal jobs have NO machine
  row, so this only fires for
  community.  Allocator can return
  this PC for the next dispatch.
end note

RL -> PG : INSERT render_telemetry

== Group rollup (step 9) ==
RL -> PG : group + jobs + output_frames + pending_alloc reads
RL -> PG : update render_groups.status (if changed)\nwrite_terminal_snapshot (if terminal)

RL --> CR
CR --> JS
JS --> R
R -->> W : 200 OK

note over W
  Community has TWO trigger paths:
  1. **PUT /status** — agent reports done first.
     update_status sets status=done synchronously,
     then notify_completion runs the rest.
  2. **POST /register-outputs** — for the agent's
     last-file path.  Same shape as Vast/Modal.
end note

@enduml


' ============================================================
' Per-fleet diff summary (cheat sheet)
' ============================================================

@startuml chunk_completion_diff

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
title Per-fleet diff at the steps that vary

note as N
  **Common to all fleets** (steps 1–5, 8–9):
    is_job_terminal check, get_raw_by_id, in_progress.release,
    mark_done, telemetry, group reconcile, terminal snapshot.
    All cheap PG hops (~50 ms total with Singapore PG).
end note

note as V #DDEEFF
  **Vast fleet** (extras):
    6a. VastClient.destroy(instance_id) — httpx DELETE, **5–30 s**
    6b. stop_monitoring — kills per-job VastInstanceMonitor thread
    Step 7: skipped (no machine row)
    Step 3 (Modal hook): skipped
end note

note as M #FFE4FF
  **Modal fleet** (extras):
    Step 3: ZREM modal:active_jobs (Redis, <5 ms)
    6a. ModalClient.cancel_job — Modal SDK gRPC, **5–20 s**
    6b. stop_monitoring — kills per-job ModalJobMonitor thread
    Step 7: skipped
end note

note as C #DDFFDD
  **Community fleet** (extras):
    6a. cancel — **no-op** (empty provider_job_id short-circuits)
    6b. stop_monitoring — **no-op** (singleton CommunityMonitor)
    Step 7: machine_repo.update_status('available') — frees the PC
    Step 3: skipped
    Trigger paths: PUT /status OR POST /register-outputs
end note

@enduml
